    <dashboard name='Story 1' type='storyboard'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true'>Customer Value Analysis</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <style />
      <size sizing-mode='automatic' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98244' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99034' x='483' y='878'>
            <zone h='4501' id='3' type-v2='title' w='99034' x='483' y='878' />
            <zone h='11087' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='99034' x='483' y='5379' />
            <zone h='82656' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='99034' x='483' y='16466'>
              <flipboard active-id='6' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point caption='1. Who are our customers?' captured-sheet='Dashboard 1' id='1' />
                  <story-point caption='2. Where are our customers?' captured-sheet='Choropleth Map' id='2' />
                  <story-point caption='3. Does income drive value?' captured-sheet='Regression Plot' id='3' />
                  <story-point caption='4. Claims by vehicle size' captured-sheet='Boxplot Analysis' id='4' />
                  <story-point caption='5. All findings together' captured-sheet='Dashboard 2' id='5' />
                  <story-point caption='6. Conclusions' captured-sheet='' id='6' />
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='23237' hidden='true' id='6' story-point-id='2' type-v2='text' w='33268' x='47146' y='33610'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0'>All customers live in 5 western states.
California (34%) and Oregon (29%) have the most customers.
Washington and Nevada have the fewest (about 9% each).</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='23237' hidden='true' id='7' story-point-id='3' type-v2='text' w='33268' x='65059' y='25726'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0'>The regression line is almost flat (R² ≈ 0).
Income does not explain Customer Lifetime Value.
The points at 0 income are mostly unemployed customers.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='26556' hidden='true' id='8' story-point-id='4' type-v2='text' w='33268' x='58563' y='39419'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Small vehicles have the highest median claim (about 451).
Medium and large vehicles are lower (about 363 and 378).
All sizes have many outliers above 1 000, so a few claims are very expensive.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='76971' id='9' story-point-id='6' type-v2='text' w='93012' x='4528' y='18465'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true'>Key findings</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>

1. We have 9 134 customers. Gender is balanced and most customers are employed and married.

2. Our customers are only in 5 western states. California and Oregon have more than 60% of them.

3. Income does not predict Customer Lifetime Value. We should not use income alone to find valuable customers.

4. Small vehicles have higher claims, and every vehicle size has some very expensive claims (outliers).</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{0ADBB892-B373-4824-9A31-2B7A9FFFBBA8}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
